        "## 18.24 Common mistakes\n",
        "\n",
        "1. **Confusing pretraining with memorization.** The objective estimates conditional token distributions.  Memorization may occur, but it is not the mathematical objective.\n",
        "2. **Ignoring masks.** The mask determines which tokens are treated as labels.\n",
        "3. **Treating KL divergence as symmetric.** In general, $D_{\\mathrm{KL}}(p\\|q)\\neq D_{\\mathrm{KL}}(q\\|p)$.\n",
        "4. **Assuming lower training loss always means better behavior.** Fine-tuning may improve one distribution while hurting another.\n",
        "5. **Equating reward with truth.** A reward model estimates preferences or scores, not a theorem about correctness.\n",
        "6. **Forgetting the reference model.** Many preference objectives are meaningful only relative to a reference distribution.\n",
        "\n",
        "## 18.25 Worked calculation\n",
        "\n",
        "Suppose a vocabulary has three tokens and the model assigns probabilities\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "p_\\theta(\\cdot\\mid c)=(0.70,0.20,0.10).\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "If the observed token is token $2$, the token loss is\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\ell=-\\log(0.20)\\approx 1.609.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "If a reference model has\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "p_0(\\cdot\\mid c)=(0.60,0.30,0.10),\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "then\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "D_{\\mathrm{KL}}(p_\\theta\\|p_0)\n",
        "=0.70\\log\\frac{0.70}{0.60}\n",
        "+0.20\\log\\frac{0.20}{0.30}\n",
        "+0.10\\log\\frac{0.10}{0.10}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Numerically,\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "D_{\\mathrm{KL}}(p_\\theta\\|p_0)\n",
        "\\approx 0.70(0.154)-0.20(0.405)+0\n",
        "\\approx 0.027.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "With $\\beta=0.5$, the KL-regularized token objective is approximately\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "1.609+0.5(0.027)=1.6225.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "The penalty is small here because the current model is close to the reference distribution.\n",
